kind: vulnerability
title: "Cisco Catalyst SD-WAN peering authentication bypass CVE-2026-20182 (CVSS 10.0), exploited and attributed to UAT-8616"
headline: "Cisco SD-WAN control-plane flaw CVE-2026-20182 lets an unauthenticated peer join and plant SSH keys; Talos ties exploitation to UAT-8616"
summary: "Cisco disclosed CVE-2026-20182 on 2026-05-14, a peering-authentication bypass in the Catalyst SD-WAN control plane (CVSS 10.0) that affects Controller, Manager and Validator regardless of configuration, with no workaround; CISA listed it as exploited the same day. Rapid7, which found it, shows an unauthenticated peer injecting an SSH key for the vmanage-admin account and reaching NETCONF, and Talos attributes the exploitation to UAT-8616 with high confidence."
event_date: 2026-05-14
priority: notable
immediate_action: null
tags:
  - vulnerabilities
  - auth-bypass
  - pre-auth
  - actively-exploited
  - cisa-kev
  - patch-available
  - nation-state
regions:
  - global
sectors: []
entities:
  - "actor:uat-8616"
techniques: [T1190, T1098.004, T1021.004, T1068]
affected_products: ["Cisco Catalyst SD-WAN Controller", "Cisco Catalyst SD-WAN Manager", "Cisco Catalyst SD-WAN Validator"]
cves:
  - id: CVE-2026-20182
    cvss: "10.0"
    epss: null
    type: auth-bypass
    vector: zero-click
    auth: pre-auth
    status:
      - exploited
      - cisa-kev
      - patch-available
    affected: "Catalyst SD-WAN Controller, Manager and Validator, all releases before the first fixed release of each train, regardless of configuration"
    fixed: "20.9.9.1; 20.12.5.4, 20.12.6.2, 20.12.7.1; 20.15.4.4, 20.15.5.2; 20.18.2.2; 26.1.1.1 (20.10 and 20.11 to 20.12.7.1; 20.13 and 20.14 to 20.15.5.2; 20.16 to 20.18.2.2; earlier than 20.9 migrate)"
sources:
